    "reply": "The evaluated genetic factors are linked to the condition Disease name: Familial cancer of breast [2]. Another associated condition is Disease name: Pancreatic cancer susceptibility 4 [4]. A relevant condition for the second locus is Disease name: Medulloblastoma [7].\n\n## BRCA1 Biological Function\nThe BRCA1 gene encodes a product that maintains genomic integrity and functions as a cancer inhibitor [24: \"maintaining genomic stability, and it also acts as a tumor suppressor\"]. This product assembles into a massive surveillance apparatus [24: \"form a large multi-subunit protein complex known as the BRCA1-associated genome surveillance complex\"]. This machinery actively drives the restoration of severed DNA strands [24: \"plays a role in transcription, DNA repair of double-stranded breaks, and recombination\"]. A related locus is Gene NCBIGene:675, name: BRCA2 DNA repair associated [6].\n\n## Cancer Risk Genetics\nGenetic variations in this locus drive a massive proportion of hereditary breast and ovarian malignancies [24: \"Mutations in this gene are responsible for approximately 40% of inherited breast cancers and more than 80% of inherited breast and ovarian cancers\"]. These variations include structural changes [24: \"disease-associated mutations, have been described for this gene\"]. Another linked condition is Disease name: Familial prostate cancer [11]. A further associated condition is Disease name: Wilms tumor 1 [13].",
    "dur": 25.611
   },
   {
    "t": 32.749,
    "model": "openrouter/google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview",
    "synth": true,
    "reasoning_param": true,
    "max_tokens": 4000,
    "ok": true,
    "prompt_tokens": 12697,
    "completion_tokens": 1943,
