    "reasoning_tokens": 1309,
    "finish": "stop",
    "openrouter_cost_usd": 0.04871,
    "reply": "The gene NCBIGene:672, known as BRCA1 DNA repair associated, is linked to Familial cancer of breast, Familial breast-ovarian cancer susceptibility 1, Pancreatic cancer susceptibility 4, and Fanconi anemia complementation group S [1][2][3][4][5]. The gene NCBIGene:675, named BRCA2 DNA repair associated, is associated with Medulloblastoma, Fanconi anemia complementation group D1, Familial breast-ovarian cancer susceptibility 2, Glioma susceptibility 3, Familial prostate cancer, Pancreatic cancer susceptibility 2, and Wilms tumor 1 [6][7][8][9][10][11][12][13]. The BRCA1 gene functions to protect the genome [24: \"maintaining genomic stability, and it also acts as a tumor suppressor\"].\n\n## BRCA1 Gene Information\n\nThe gene is identified by the gene symbol: BRCA1 and gene name: BRCA1 [14][18]. It is documented in OMIM as BRCA1 DNA REPAIR-ASSOCIATED PROTEIN; BRCA1 and is involved in DNA repair and double-strand break repair via homologous recombination [17][27][21]. Known variants include NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.5243_5277+2788del, NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.5277+2916_5277+2946delinsGG, and NG_005905.2:g.(147057_150288)_(160933_166866)del [16][23][29]. The gene encodes a protein that participates in several critical processes [24: \"role in transcription, DNA repair of double-stranded breaks, and recombination\"].\n\n## Related Clinical Trials\n\nSeveral clinical studies investigate these genes, including Germline BRCA1 and BRCA2 Mutations in Jewish Women Affected by Breast Cancer [19]. Other trials are BRCA1 Haploinsufficiency and Gene Expression and Study to Evaluate Treatment Customized According to RAP80 and BRCA1 in Patients With Advanced Lung Carcinoma [25][30]. Defective variants are heavily tied to hereditary cancers [24: \"responsible for approximately 40% of inherited breast cancers and more than 80% of inherited breast and ovarian cancers\"].\n\n## Literature and Research\n\nRecent literature includes Publication pmid: 35263698 and Publication pmid: 35432218 [20][26]. Specific studies cover PTEN alterations in sporadic and BRCA1-associated triple negative breast carcinomas. and BRCA1: An Endocrine and Metabolic Regulator. [15][22]. Additional research explores the microenvironment in Preneoplastic stromal cells promote BRCA1-mediated breast tumorigenesis. [28].",
    "dur": 13.213
   }
